; FM3 as a thick pad on one channel: every operator gets its own pitch. The
; progression plays twice: first the operators in plain unison, then pulled
; apart. Two carriers play the root a semitone apart (-50 and +50 cents) and
; the bass sits 30 sharp; the fifth glides. Each detuned operator also swings
; on a wide vibrato of its own speed (:pitch+ adds to its offset), so the
; gap between them keeps opening and closing, from unison to a whole tone.
(def-fm pad4 init-fm :alg 7 :fb 0
  :ar1 14 :ar2 14 :ar3 12 :ar4 10
  :tl1 12 :tl2 12 :tl3 16 :tl4 14
  :rr1 5 :rr2 5 :rr3 5 :rr4 5)

(def chords c a- f g)

(fm3 pad4)
(fm3-1 :tempo 84 :oct 4 :len 1 chords
  :pitch -50 (macro :pitch+ (sin -50..50 :len 1)) chords)
(fm3-2 :oct 4 :len 1 chords
  :pitch 50 (macro :pitch+ (sin -50..50 :len 3/2)) chords)
(fm3-3 :oct 4 :len 1 g e- c d
  (glide 4) g e- c d)
(fm3-4 :oct 3 :len 1 chords
  :pitch 30 (macro :pitch+ (sin -30..30 :len 2)) chords)
